===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who has [[special]] [[knowledge]] about the [[inner]] workings of a [[group]], [[organization]], or [[institution]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2 Jul 1923|title=‘Big Board’ Failures|titleurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20080214133603/http://www.time.com/time/magazine/article/0,9171,716015,00.html|journal=Time
|passage=Heavy losses were sustained in Simms Petroleum, which took a greater toll from supposed "Wall Street '''insiders'''" than from the general public.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=19 Dec 2007|author=Jonathan Clayton|title=Profile: Zuma charmed wives and a nation|titleurl=http://www.timesonline.co.uk/tol/news/world/africa/article3070220.ece|journal=Times of London|location=UK
|passage=He is also an astute ANC '''insider''' who spent ten years on Robben Island alongside Nelson Mandela and the other “grandees” of the movement.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=31 July 2018|author=Julia Carrie Wong|title=What is QAnon? Explaining the bizarre rightwing conspiracy theory
|work=w:The Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2018/jul/30/qanon-4chan-rightwing-conspiracy-theory-explained-trump|text= In a thread called “Calm Before the Storm”, and in subsequent posts, Q established his legend as a government '''insider''' with top security clearance who knew the truth about a secret struggle for power involving Donald Trump, the “deep state”, Robert Mueller, the Clintons, pedophile rings, and other stuff.}}
# A person who is within an [[enclosed]] [[space]].
#* {{RQ:Melville Redburn|33|passage=To the '''insider''', the ceiling is like a small firmament twinkling with astral radiations.}}

